uting", "vLLM multi-cluster", "AI cost per customer", "SaaS AI infrastructure", "fractional CTO United States", "inference portability"], "faq": [["Why would a SaaS company need AI capacity in more than one region?", "Because capacity in a single region can be hard to expand when demand outruns supply, and new data centres can be delayed. Serving from several regions and providers keeps AI features available and gives room to negotiate."], ["Does multi-region serving mean running everything everywhere?", "No. In this design, a primary region carries most traffic, a secondary region and managed APIs absorb overflow and failures, and routing decides per request based on capacity, latency and data rules."], ["How do you keep costs under control across providers?", "Record model, provider, tokens and customer on every request, and report cost per feature and per customer. That shows where capacity is worth reserving and where overflow pricing is acceptable."]], "related": ["/fractional-cto-united-states/", "/ai-architect/", "/fractional-cto/"], "citations": [{"title": "Voters rebuff data centers in every ballot measure except one during the 2026 midterms", "url": "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/04/data-center-ballot-measures-2026-midterm.html", "publisher": "CNBC", "date": "4 Nov 2026"}, {"title": "2026 election results show widespread opposition to AI data centers", "url": "https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/2026-election-results-show-widespread-opposition-to-ai-data-centers/", "publisher": "Scientific American", "date": "Nov 2026"}, {"title": "Microsoft's cloud growth accelerates, and so too does the spending", "url": "https://fortune.com/2026/10/28/microsofts-cloud-growth-accelerates-and-so-too-does-the-spending/", "publisher": "Fortune", "date": "28 Oct 2026"}, {"title": "TeraWulf Secures Google Credit Backstop for Project Financing in Support of $19 Billion Anthropic Lease; Executes Definitive Fluor EPC Agreement", "url": "https://investors.terawulf.com/news-